WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Engine foundations. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Name assemblies; label energy paths

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: An engine is a chain of jobs: air and fuel release energy, pistons move, and the crankshaft delivers rotation. Cooling and lubrication support that process.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Trace the path: fuel/air → cylinder pressure → piston motion → crankshaft rotation.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Sort components by function

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Name assemblies; label energy paths
